    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
      children: "Lean manufacturing uses the principle of \"andon cords\" - mechanisms by which any worker can immediately halt the production line when a defect is detected. The software equivalent is making the health of your system visible and giving every engineer the ability to trigger an incident response. This means shared dashboards showing error rates, latency percentiles, and deployment status for all services. It means alerting pipelines that route to the people with the context to act. It means deployment histories that are accessible without digging through audit logs."
    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
      children: "When work is visible, problems are detected earlier, the right people are notified faster, and the cognitive model that engineers have of the production system improves over time. Visibility also changes behavior: when engineers can see the real-time impact of their deployments, they take more care in how they deploy. The feedback loop tightens."
    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.h3, {
